; Stream hits.parquet into a splayed on-disk table under ./hits.
;
; `.parquet.splayed` reads the file row group by row group and writes one column
; file per field plus the `.sym` dictionary, without materialising the whole
; table in memory. The column names come from the file; `hits-types` gives the
; native type of each column in the file's order.
(load "create.rfl")
(.parquet.splayed hits-types "hits.parquet" "hits")
(exit 0)
